This project builds on, and links against or downloads, the following software.
None of it is redistributed in this repository except where stated.

- Kokoro-82M model and voices (Apache-2.0), https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M.
  The ONNX export and voice pack are downloaded by scripts/download_models.sh from
  the kokoro-onnx releases.
- kokoro-onnx (MIT), https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx, used as a git
  submodule in third_party/kokoro-onnx.
- mlir-aie / IRON and the Peano compiler (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, Copyright
  Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.), https://github.com/Xilinx/mlir-aie. Cloned and
  installed by scripts/setup_ironenv.sh. kernels/conv1d_npu.py and kernels/snake_npu.py
  are derived from its programming_examples (whole_array matrix multiplication) and keep
  that license.
- AMD XRT (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/Xilinx/XRT. pyxrt is built from its source by
  scripts/build_pyxrt.sh.
- ONNX Runtime (MIT), https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime. The C API headers are
  downloaded by scripts/fetch_ort_headers.sh.
- onnxruntime-extensions is not used.

The investigation that led to this project started from Unicorn-Commander/magic-unicorn-tts
(Apache-2.0). None of its code is used here; see UPSTREAM_BUGS.md.
